The UDR forces all outbound traffic through the firewall for inspection and logging.

Hands-on Lab 1: Create a Route Table
Azure Portal

Create:

Setting	Value
Name	rt-web-dev
Resource Group	rg-az400-dev
Region	Central India
Azure CLI
az network route-table create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --name rt-web-dev

Verify:

az network route-table list --output table
Hands-on Lab 2: Create a User Defined Route

Example route:

Destination:
0.0.0.0/0

Next Hop:
Internet

CLI:

az network route-table route create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --route-table-name rt-web-dev \
  --name DefaultRoute \
  --address-prefix 0.0.0.0/0 \
  --next-hop-type Internet

In real production environments, this next hop is often Azure Firewall or a Virtual Appliance, not the Internet.

Hands-on Lab 3: Associate Route Table

Associate it with web-subnet:

az network vnet subnet update \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --vnet-name vnet-az400-dev \
  --name web-subnet \
  --route-table rt-web-dev
