Azure Key Vault

Secrets are accessed entirely over the private Azure network.

Benefits
No public exposure
Private IP access
Higher security
Supports regulatory compliance
Service Endpoint vs Private Endpoint
Feature	Service Endpoint	Private Endpoint
Public IP still exists	✅ Yes	❌ No (can disable public access)
Uses Private IP	❌ No	✅ Yes
Works over Azure backbone	✅ Yes	✅ Yes
Highest Security	Good	Best
DNS Changes Required	No	Usually Yes (Private DNS Zone)
Which Should You Choose?

Use Service Endpoints when:

Simplicity is sufficient.
Public endpoints are acceptable with subnet restrictions.

Use Private Endpoints when:

Accessing sensitive services (Key Vault, SQL Database, Storage).
Public access must be disabled.
Compliance or strict security requirements exist.
